[[Metz]] believed that Vigilante was originally used by a very evil Seeker and thus would easily bond to a Seeker with a strong dark side. {{source|Den vs Harrison}}

[[Lok Lambert]] and [[Sophie Casterwill]] were tasked to deliver Vigilante's Amulet to [[Huntik Foundation Dutch HQ]]. However they were intercepted by the [[Blood Spiral]] and Lok ended up dropping the Amulet during a battle on the [[Erasmus Bridge]]. [[Den Fears]] then fought [[Harrison Fears]] for the Amulet, and the Titan sensed and ended up bonding with Den to become his first and primary Titan. Vigilante then fought against [[Harlekin]], but with Den choked and beaten by Harrison and unable to concentrate, Vigilante was sent back to his Amulet. {{source|Den vs Harrison}}

Den used Vigilante during the Huntik team's attempt to rescue [[Focauld Casterwill]] from [[Kiel]] and [[Marduk]] in the [[Cloisters]]. He was, however, defeated by Marduk's [[Cerberus]]. {{source|The Casterwill Connection}}

In Hamelin, Den invoked Vigilante to help [[Sophie Casterwill]] against two [[Suits]]. Charged up with a power boost from [[Cherit]], Vigilante fought and defeated [[Shadow Agent]]. {{source|Gremlow Infestation!}}

Den attempted to invoke Vigilante against [[Wilder]] in [[the Professor's castle]] but Wilder kicked the Amulet out of his hand. {{source|An Ally from the Organization}}

At the [[Blood Spiral Base]], after faltering during his final battle with his brother, Harrison, Den sensed Vigilante becoming Powerbonded, reminding him that him not to let his friends down. After invoking Powerbonded Vigilante, Den merged with him using his new Cindercloak ability and fought and defeated [[Antedeluvian|Powerbonded Antedeluvian]]. Before he could defeat Harrison however, Vigilante was disrupted by falling rocks and sent back to his Amulet. {{source|Lok and the Betrayer}}

Den invoked Powerbonded Vigilante in Japan where he fought alongside [[Baselaird|Powerbonded Baselaird]] to defeat two [[Shadow Agent]] Titans when they arrived at [[Emi]]'s house. {{source|The Guardian of Yonaguni}}

Vigilante became Powerbonded with Den during his final battle with his brother, Harrison. Using his new '''Cindercloak''' ability, Den was able to merge with Vigilante in a similar fashion to how [[Lok Lambert]] merges with Powerbonded [[Kipperin]]. Powerbonded Vigilante can then separate himself from his Seeker in order to provide protection, such as when he used this ability to protect Den when the ruins of the [[Spiral Mark]] started to collapse. Together, Den and Vigilante's sword strikes are powerful enough to defeat [[Antedeluvian|Powerbonded Antedeluvian]].{{source|Lok and the Betrayer}} Powerbonded Vigilante's other new abilities include:

*'''Counterattack''' - swiftly strikes an enemy after defending their attack. {{source|The Guardian of Yonaguni}}
* '''Cross defense''' - crosses his two swords to block an attack. {{source|The Guardian of Yonaguni}}

